.omo
/target

# Release archives and the unpacked artifact `make smoke-artifact` exercises.
# Build outputs, never source.
/dist

# Reference clones of the projects this port draws on (~570 MB). Task 1 copies
# them here from /tmp so the References lines in .omo/plans stop dangling; they
# are other people's repositories and must never enter this history.
.omo/refs/

# Per-task verification transcripts. Originally ignored as "local proof, not
# shared source"; that was wrong once the gates became expensive. Todo 88's
# transcript is the only record of a ~100-minute paired memory measurement, 89's
# of a 2-hour soak, and 90/113/114's of results no reader can reproduce cheaply.
# Agents force-added the five costliest for exactly that reason, which left the
# directory half-tracked and silently dropped todo 112's file. Decisive argument:
# untracked files do not propagate into a `git worktree`, so a worktree-based
# Final-Wave audit would see NO evidence at all. 1.5 MB for a durable audit trail
# is the cheaper trade. Only the throwaway generator scripts stay ignored.
.omo/evidence/*.sh
.omo/evidence/*.mjs
.omo/evidence/*.json

.omo/run-continuation/
.omo/delegated-runtime/

*.pdb
.DS_Store
